\title{Full Pinning and Strict Decay on the Abelian Splitting-Type Ladder}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{September 3, 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We study the information carried by residue data about the splitting behaviour of primes in
abelian number fields, organised as a ladder of real cyclotomic fields $\Q(\zeta_f)^{+}$ of prime
degree. We prove a universal pinning theorem: for any finite abelian group $G$ and any subgroup
$H$, the type read-out $u \mapsto \ord(uH)$ in $G/H$ is a function of the class $uH$, so the
conditional entropy of the type given the class vanishes identically and the mutual information
equals the full type entropy. We then prove that pinning is exactly measurability: the conditional
entropy $H(T \mid k)$ vanishes if and only if the channel $k$ determines $T$ pointwise, the
quantitative core being that a non-constant read-out on a finite set has strictly positive counting
entropy. At degree $11$, realised by $\Q(\zeta_{23})^{+}$, we establish the arithmetic law
($p$ splits completely iff $p \equiv \pm 1 \bmod 23$), the certified bracket
$0.4394 < H(T_{11}) < 0.4396$, and an explicit failing channel: the quadratic character mod $23$,
which merges the split class $1$ with the inert class $2$ (as $5^2 \equiv 2$) and in fact carries
exactly zero information. We prove the exact $\Bin(2,1/q)$ law for the semiprime split count, with
counts $\big((q-1)^2, 2(q-1), 1\big)$ out of $q^2$, and a closed form for the split-count channel
giving $\Isplit(11) = \log_2 11 + (180\log_2 3 - 210\log_2 5 - 210)/121 = 0.05190\ldots$, certified
in $(0.0516, 0.0521)$. Finally we determine the shape of the ladder: the sandwich
$\log_2 q/q \le H(T_q) \le (\log_2 q + 1/\ln 2)/q$, and the exact derivative
$h'(x) = -\ln(x-1)/(x^2\ln 2)$ of the real interpolation, whence strict antitonicity on
$[2,\infty)$ and strict decay along the primes, with degree $2$ the unique rung carrying a full bit.
\end{abstract}

